<description>
Complete every colored fragment into a translated copy of the unique largest foreground template.

Input structure
- A uniform background contains one complete monochromatic template mask and smaller same-orientation fragments in other colors.
- A color may contain more than one separated fragment; each fragment has at least two pixels.
- All completed copies fit inside the grid and do not overlap other foreground pixels.

Rule
- Use the unique foreground color with the most pixels as the template mask.
- For each other color, find the unique minimum set of translated template placements whose existing template cells cover that color's input pixels.
- Paint every cell of those placements with that color, leaving the template and background otherwise unchanged.

Key insight
The incomplete colors are partial masks of the same template; their existing pixels act as anchors that determine where the missing cells must be filled.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "non-template color mask s, possibly split into multiple fragments",
  "dst": "translated copies d of the unique largest foreground template mask",
  "match_cond": "d contains the observed s pixels; choose the unique minimum non-overlapping set of d per color",
  "transform": "paint every cell of each matched d with s.color; leave the template unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22-30 rows x 22-30 cols (square)
  background: single color filling most of the grid; density of all fg cells <7%
  template:
    shape: irregular asymmetric mask, 5-8 cells, bbox 3-4 rows x 3-5 cols
    connectivity: 8-connected but NOT 4-connected (has diagonal-only joins) [observed]
    color: unique fg color with strictly the most pixels; appears exactly once
  fragments:
    count: 4-7 distinct non-template fg colors
    copies_per_color: usually 1, occasionally 2 (total copies incl template 5-9)
    anchor_pixels_per_copy: 2-3 (subset of the template's cell positions at that placement)
    anchor_pixels_per_color: 2-5 total across all copies of that color
    each anchor pixel set must uniquely determine a minimum non-overlapping cover of template placements
  layout:
    all completed copies (template + fragments) are non-overlapping
    min Chebyshev distance between any two different-color groups >= 3
    all copies fit entirely within the grid
  output:
    for each fragment color, fill in the remaining template cells at each placement
    template and background unchanged; only bg cells become fragment-colored

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (22-30, square) and background color
    2. Design an irregular template mask (5-8 cells in a 3-4 x 3-5 bbox, 8-connected but not 4-connected, asymmetric)
    3. Pick N=5-9 distinct fg colors; one is the template color, the rest are fragment colors
    4. Place all N translated copies of the template on the grid such that no two overlap and min Chebyshev gap >= 3; all within bounds. This is the output state
    5. Assign fragment colors to non-template copies (most get 1 copy; optionally 1 color gets 2)
    6. For each fragment copy, select 2-3 anchor pixels from its template cells; remove the rest (set to bg) to get the input. Ensure per-color anchors uniquely determine the cover
    7. Verify the template color has strictly more pixels than any single fragment color in the input
```
