 136:     - Treat wall pixels as blocked and every other pixel as passable.
 137:     - Find every passable pixel that lies on a shortest 4-connected path between the two endpoint components.
 138:     - Also fill any framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that intersects that shortest-path mask.
 139: 
 140:     Key insight
 141:     - Shortest paths identify the route through open connector corridors, while the wall-bordered square rooms need to be expanded from the route centerline to their full interior.
